{
  "summary": "You produced a well-structured, fluent report that identifies the core ethical dilemma and balances commercial pressures against public safety. Your introduction and ethical framework alignment are strong. To raise your work to the highest rubric tiers, ensure all required structural sections (such as the abstract) and visual aids are included, expand decision-making recommendations to cover multiple distinct stakeholders, and verify the accuracy of external case study facts and arithmetic.",
  "next_steps": [
    "Include an opening abstract (~150 words) and integrate competent visual elements, such as stakeholder impact matrices or decision trees, to satisfy C5 requirements.",
    "Broaden your concluding recommendations beyond Rachel to explicitly advise other key stakeholders, such as company executives and the client health department.",
    "Fact-check external evidence and technical data carefully, correcting the Volkswagen case details and the calculation of 1% of 5,000 servers."
  ],
  "criteria": {
    "C1": "You achieved Excellent by clearly contextualising the engineering dilemma and identifying key stakeholders like Rachel, the company, and end-users in your 'INTRODUCTION'.",
    "C2": "You provided balanced arguments in 'DISCUSSION: To Ship or Not to Ship'. To reach Excellent, expand your recommendations in 'RECOMMENDATION' beyond Rachel to address distinct actions for several different stakeholders.",
    "C3": "Your argument in 'The Most Ethical Path' prioritises safety effectively. To reach Excellent, resolve the contradiction in 'RECOMMENDATION' where Rachel is advised to accept the contract despite severe defect risks.",
    "C4": "You effectively cited the NHS case and professional codes. To reach Very Good or Excellent, broaden your references and ensure technical accuracy regarding external cases (e.g., VW diesel emissions, not EV crash tests).",
    "C5": "Your writing is fluent and readable. To reach Very Good or Excellent, you must include the missing abstract and competently incorporate visual elements such as tables or figures to support your discussion."
  }
}
